{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"702620138662527047","content":"Web wipes sweat from their brow, and looks up and the fruits of their labor. Web is crawling with spiders, but there are scores more on the thing they are looking at.  It is a massive spiderweb, stretching the entire circumference of the huge sewer tunnel it rests in. It is colorful, made of a variety of yarns and threads, stitched together or woven by Web and their 'disciples'. Web nods at the druid standing next to them with parchment and ink, and gratefully accepts the drawing she holds out to them. \nWeb looks up at the massive web once more, taking in its beauty. \"A fine way to leave home. It's everything I hoped it would be.\" An insectoid woman comes up and places her hand on Web's shoulder. ||It is time to say your goodbyes, weave-master.|| She says in Kraul. Web replies kindly ||have I truly earned that title? I am yet so young.|| \n||Of course.|| Ishka replies, gesturing up at the massive web above them. ||Does such a work not deserve a title?||\nWeb grins at this. ||I suppose it does, spin-mother Ishka. I suppose it does.||\nThe massive web is crawling with spiders of different shapes and ages, all of which seem to turn towards Web as they turn to leave. A massive echoing chirr can be heard as all the spiders vocalize at once. \nWeb tears up, grinning sadly. ||I won't ever forget you, either|| they say, before following Ishka down an adjacent pipe.\nAnd with that, the spider god's final gift to their London children is given.","created_at":"2020-07-25T00:34:10.774000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"736380744468791407","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
